post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  The menu entry belongs to a single user's config, so it is not installed
  system-wide. Run this once, as the user who should get it:

      omarchy-better-passwordless-sudo --setup-menu

  It then appears under: Omarchy menu -> Setup -> Security -> Passwordless Sudo

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  If the menu entry ever goes missing, put it back with:

      omarchy-better-passwordless-sudo --setup-menu

MSG
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  Remove the per-user menu entry before this package goes away, while the
  command still exists:

      omarchy-better-passwordless-sudo --remove-menu

MSG
}
